Here is my forecast:

{"reasoning": "The user’s described breakthrough has already been achieved as reported in Science very recently (within the last few days): ionic covalent organic frameworks showing continuous, reversible pore tuning between 2.9 Å and 4.0 Å over 100 thermal cycles with resolution below 0.2 Å, enabling selective gas separations ([science.org](https://www.science.org/doi/pdf/10.1126/science.adj8791)). Therefore, the breakthrough has already occurred and been publicly demonstrated this year.", "answer": "2026-05", "confidence": 0.90, "sources": ["https://www.science.org/doi/pdf/10.1126/science.adj8791"]}

Explanation: A recent Science article reports exactly the described capability: continuous, reversible tunability of dynamic pores between 2.9 and 4.0 angstroms with resolution under 0.2 angstroms over 100 thermal cycles, enabling selective recognition and separation of gas mixtures ([science.org](https://www.science.org/doi/pdf/10.1126/science.adj8791)). Given the crawling date was “2 days ago” and the current date is May 2, 2026, the public demonstration is effectively now (May 2026).

